// A5 production serial agent loop (script-owned).
//
// The exported `run(context)` is a step function: ONE typed context map in,
// ONE discriminated decision map out. The loop state machine, canonical
// LlmRequest construction, provider/profile dispatch, tool registry +
// approval + dispatch, event emission, and durable compaction execution all
// live in this module (and the harness/llm/storage modules it composes).
// Rust (AgentService) owns lifecycle (timeout, cancel, retry sleep),
// capability composition (http/io/sqlite policy), approval persistence, and
// durable terminal sequencing; it never parses provider wire and never
// writes agent policy.
//
// The loop runs internally across provider calls and tool rounds and yields
// a decision ONLY when an external service side effect is required:
//
//   run.completed     -> service commits the terminal exactly once (the
//                        final text-only assistant message is service-owned)
//   run.failed        -> service commits the typed terminal exactly once
//   retry             -> service sleeps delay_ms (bounded backoff) and
//                        re-invokes with retry_count + 1, same turn
//   approval.wait     -> service persists the approval durably, parks the
//                        run (waiting_approval), and resumes exactly once
//   compact           -> service transitions the run to 'compacting' and
//                        re-invokes with phase "compacting"
//   compacted         -> service transitions back to 'running' and
//                        re-invokes phase "start" with the trimmed messages
//   compact.failed    -> service transitions back to 'running'; the typed
//                        failure is durable and the history is untouched
//   parallel.handoff / subagent.handoff -> typed, executable:false; the
//                        serial loop never invents parallel/subagent
//                        outcomes (A6 native supervision needs the A7
//                        run-admission interface)
//   rejected          -> typed unknown-phase/state failure
//
// Every decision that must continue carries the full loop state (messages,
// turn, retry_count, last_text, tool_calls, tool_index, plan) so the
// service can re-invoke; the service copies typed fields only.
//
// Context (flat, typed; missing fields fall back to documented defaults):
//
//   run_id, session_id: string
//   phase: "start" | "approval.resume" | "compacting"
//   turn: int            completed model rounds so far (0 initially)
//   retry_count: int     retries consumed on the current turn
//   max_turns: int       turns allowed before the run terminates (bounded)
//   max_retries: int     retries allowed per turn
//   model: string        model name carried by model.* event descriptors
//   provider: string     adapter/profile name ("openai_chat" |
//                        "openai_responses" | "anthropic_messages" |
//                        "openrouter" | "deepseek" | "opencode_zen" |
//                        "opencode_go" | "custom")
//   provider_options: map  {base_url, api_key, model, ...} for direct
//                        adapters; profile modules read them from the
//                        canonical request
//   system_prompt: string (prepended as a system message when non-empty)
//   messages: array     canonical message history (seeded from the durable
//                        session by the service; appended inline by the
//                        loop)
//   config: map         {base_retry_delay_ms, max_retry_delay_ms,
//                        max_context_messages, retained_tail,
//                        approval_mode, native_hard_deny, stream,
//                        parallel, task, max_output_tokens, state_db,
//                        now_ms}
//   approval: map       (phase "approval.resume") {approval_id,
//                        tool_call_id, tool_name, arguments, risk_class,
//                        resolved, reason}
//   tool_calls: array   (phase "approval.resume") the round's call list
//   tool_index: int     (phase "approval.resume") the pending call index
//   plan: map           (phase "compacting") the compact.plan decision
//
// Compiler-contract notes (pinned core fd4b570, B1-B4 fixed): cross-module
// script calls are placed at function top level, in expression-if branches,
// or inside `while` bodies; annotated locals whose initializer type the
// checker cannot prove live in helpers with declared return types;
// `json::encode` / `json::decode` results cross boundaries through declared
// `string` / `map` / `array` returns.

